      "title": "Data Analyst - Inland Empire Mental Health Training & Integration Center",
      "description": "Data Analyst - Inland Empire Mental Health Training & Integration Center | Job Opportunities British English CA English Czech Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Hungarian Italian Japanese Korean Polish Português do Brasil Romanian Swedish Thai U.S. English Vietnamese 简体中文 繁體中文 Find Opportunities U.S. English Sign In Accessibility Note If you are a job seeker with a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to apply for one of our jobs, you will find the contact information to request the appropriate accommodation by visiting the following our Accessibility Accomodation for Applicants page. Visit page Dismiss Data Analyst - Inland Empire Mental Health Training & Integration Center Share Post on X Apply now Job Details Posting Details Posted on October 30, 2026 Locations Showing 1 location California - Redlands University of Redlands 1200 E Colton Ave Redlands, CA 92374, USA California - Redlands University of Redlands 1200 E Colton Ave Redlands, CA 92374, USA +0 more locations less locations On-site Staff Part-Time Requisition #: DATAA001864 Description Position Code: 8067 DEPARTMENT/ADMINISTRATION: Inland Empire Mental Health Training & Integration Center (IE MHTIC) POSITION : Temporary (2 months), Part-time (10 Hours) Through December 31, 2026, or until grant funding is exhausted, whichever occurs first. SALARY RANGE: $16.90-$16.90 HIRING RANGE: Anticipated hiring range is near or at the minimum of the classification, commensurate with candidate's education, experience, skills, and training. INTRODUCTORY PERIOD: Six (6) Months AVAILABLE: Immediately POSTING DATE: October 30th , 2026 APPLICATION DEADLINE: Open Until Filled, Apply Immediately. Definition of Classification: The Inland Empire Mental Health Training & Integration Center (IE MHTIC) at the University of Redlands seeks a detail-oriented Data Analyst to support research, evaluation, and data management activities across projects focused on mental health and school-based services. Working under the supervision of the IE MHTIC research team, the Data Analyst will support the organization, management, cleaning, and analysis of research datasets. This position offers hands-on experience with applied research, quantitative data analysis, and research reporting while contributing to projects that support mental health research and community well-being. The ideal candidate has a foundational understanding of quantitative data and research methods, strong attention to detail, and an interest in applied research. Experience with statistical software is preferred but not required. Training on project-specific software, procedures, and analytic approaches will be provided. Duties and Responsibilities: The duties and responsibilities include, but are not limited to, the following: Data Management: Organize, maintain, clean, and prepare research datasets for analysis. Data Quality Assurance: Review datasets for inconsistencies, missing data, errors, and other data-quality issues; assist with identifying and resolving discrepancies. Data Analysis: Conduct basic quantitative data analyses under the guidance of the research team. Research Reporting: Assist with preparing tables, figures, descriptive summaries, and other materials for research reports and project deliverables. Research Support: Contribute to data-related activities across ongoing research, assessment, and evaluation projects. Data Integrity and Confidentiality: Follow established procedures for data security, confidentiality, documentation, and responsible research data management. Qualifications Guidelines: Any combination of experience/training/education equivalent to, but not limited to, the following: Foundational understanding of quantitative data and research methods. Strong attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy. Organizational skills and the ability to manage research data systematically. Ability to work independently on assigned tasks while communicating questions, challenges, and progress to the research team. Willingness to learn new software, data management procedures, and analytic techniques. Ability to maintain confidentiality and follow established data management protocols. Minimum Qualifications: Foundational understanding of quantitative data and research methods. Strong attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy. Organizational skills and the ability to manage research data systematically. Ability to work independently on assigned tasks while communicating questions, challenges, and progress to the research team. Willingness to learn new software, data management procedures, and analytic techniques. Ability to maintain confidentiality and follow established data management protocols. Preferred Experience working with research datasets or supporting research projects. Familiarity with statistical software such as SPSS, Mplus, R, or similar programs. Coursework or experience in psychology, counseling, education, public health, social sciences, statistics, or a related field. Interest in mental health research, program evaluation, or school-based services. Advanced statistical analysis experience is not required. Training and supervision will be provided for project-specific responsibilities. Physical Requirements/Working Conditions: Working Conditions: Working Conditions: Standard office and field setting. Duties performed are in an office environment while sitting at a desk or computer workstation or in meetings. Duties are also performed in various outdoor settings, including high elevation mountains, deserts, and other potentially hazardous environments. The position requires working evenings, weekends, and some holidays. Physical Demands: Incumbents regularly sit for long periods; walk short distances on a regular basis; travel to various locations to attend meetings and conduct work; use hands and fingers to operate an electronic keyboard or other office machines; reach with hands and arms; stoop or kneel or crouch to file;  speak clearly and distinctly to answer telephones and to provide information; see to read fine print and operate computer; hear and understand voices over telephone and in person; and lift, carry and/or move objects weighing up to 20 pounds. TO APPLY: A resume/CV and cover letter are required. In compliance with The Americans with Disabilities Act, if selected for the interview process and accommodations are needed, please call (909) 748-8040. If you are unable to complete an application due to a disability, contact us at (909) 748-8040 to ask for accommodation or an alternative application process. BACKGROUND CHECK: Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Offers are conditional and may be rescinded if disqualifying information is found or if information was withheld or falsified. Current employees may be affected if the check is not satisfactorily completed. DRIVER’S LICENSE: Certain positions require a valid driver’s license and enrollment in the DMV Government Employer Pull Notice Program to verify license status and driving record. PHYSICAL/PSYCHOLOGICAL EXAMS: Select positions (e.g., Public Safety, Facilities, Student Affairs, Athletics, ITS) require a pre-employment physical exam, including the ability to lift 50+ lbs. Public Safety Officers must also pass a psychological evaluation. FOR MORE INFORMATION VISIT Human Resources (redlands.edu) SUBMISSION OF A RESUME OR APPLICATION INDICATES AGREEMENT THAT THE UNIVERSITY MAY VERIFY ANY AND ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED THEREIN. MEMBERS OF UNDERREPRESENTED GROUPS ARE ENCOURAGED TO APPLY. AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications Equal Opportunity Employer/Protected Veterans/Individuals with Disabilities This employer is required to notify all applicants of their rights pursuant to federal employment laws.\nFor further information, please review the Know Your Rights notice from the Department of Labor. AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
