    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/UNI1089UOR/JobBoard/6af23b67-9dd3-4a6a-bda1-676b92a4fcb4/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=0eda1e72-6db0-4cd9-97a2-c24361cf920c": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Prospect Research and Management",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Prospect Research and Management | Job Opportunities British English CA English Czech Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Hungarian Italian Japanese Korean Polish Português do Brasil Romanian Swedish Thai U.S. English Vietnamese 简体中文 繁體中文 Find Opportunities U.S. English Sign In Accessibility Note If you are a job seeker with a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to apply for one of our jobs, you will find the contact information to request the appropriate accommodation by visiting the following our Accessibility Accomodation for Applicants page. Visit page Dismiss Assistant Director of Prospect Research and Management Share Post on X Apply now Job Details Posting Details Posted on September 25, 2026 Locations Showing 1 location California - Redlands University of Redlands 1200 E Colton Ave Redlands, CA 92374, USA California - Redlands University of Redlands 1200 E Colton Ave Redlands, CA 92374, USA +0 more locations less locations On-site Admin Full-Time Requisition #: ASSIS001848 Description Position Code: 8048 DEPARTMENT/ADMINISTRATION: Office of Advancement POSITION : Administrative, Exempt (12 months), Full-time (40 Hours) SALARY RANGE: $70,304-70,304 HIRING RANGE: Anticipated hiring range is near or at the minimum of the classification, commensurate with candidate's education, experience, skills, and training. INTRODUCTORY PERIOD: Twelve (12) Months AVAILABLE: Immediately POSTING DATE: September 24 , 2026 APPLICATION DEADLINE: Open Until Filled, Apply Immediately. Definition of Classification: The Assistant Director of Prospect Research and Management (ADPRM) serves as a strategic partner to Advancement leadership by providing prospect research, wealth intelligence, portfolio analysis, and prospect management support to advance fundraising priorities and institutional goals. The ADPRM is responsible for identifying, researching, analyzing, and evaluating prospective donors using a variety of biographical, philanthropic, financial, and public information sources. This position works closely with gift officers, Advancement Operations, and departmental leadership to develop prospect pipelines, enhance fundraising strategies, and support major gift cultivation and solicitation efforts. The ADPRM helps ensure that Advancement staff have access to accurate, timely, and actionable prospect intelligence to support effective donor engagement and fundraising success. Duties and Responsibilities: This position serves as a key resource within Advancement Operations by providing comprehensive prospect research, portfolio management support, wealth screening analysis, and fundraising intelligence. The role works closely with Advancement leadership, gift officers, and Advancement Services staff to identify new major gift prospects, assess philanthropic capacity, evaluate donor engagement, and support strategic fundraising initiatives. Responsibilities include conducting in-depth research and analysis, preparing prospect profiles and briefings, managing prospect pipelines, and monitoring fundraising portfolios to maximize development officer effectiveness. The position also supports prospect management processes, develops data-driven recommendations, and helps maintain research standards, confidentiality, and compliance with ethical research practices and institutional data governance policies. The duties and responsibilities include, but are not limited to, the following: Prospect Research and Analysis: • Conduct comprehensive research and analysis on individuals, corporations, foundations, and organizations to assess philanthropic capacity, affinity, and inclination to support the institution. • Prepare detailed prospect profiles, briefing materials, relationship maps, and research reports for Advancement leadership, gift officers, and institutional executives. • Identify and qualify new major gift, principal gift, and planned giving prospects through proactive research and data analysis. • Utilize public records, subscription research tools, wealth screening resources, and internal systems to gather and evaluate prospect information. • Support wealth screening projects and assist in evaluating screening results and recommendations. • Maintain current knowledge of wealth indicators, philanthropic giving patterns, and prospect research best practices. • Promote ethical research practices and ensure compliance with institutional policies and professional prospect research standards. • Ensure prospect research records are accurate, complete, and appropriately maintained within the CRM. Prospect Management: • Partner with development officers and Advancement leadership to develop and maintain prospect portfolios. • Conduct regular portfolio reviews to reflect pipeline movement and ensure updates are captured in the CRM. • Assist with the development and maintenance of prospect management policies, procedures, and business processes. • Collaborate with Advancement staff to ensure prospect records accurately reflect current research findings and engagement activity. Reporting and Analytics: • Maintain reports and dashboards related to prospect identification, portfolio performance, fundraising activity, and pipeline metrics. • Assist the Sr. Dir. of Advancement Operations & Prospect Research in monitoring key performance indicators related to major gifts and fundraising outcomes. • Coordinate recurring prospect and fundraising performance reports for Advancement leadership and frontline fundraising staff. • Performs other duties as assigned by the Sr. Director of Advancement Operations and Prospect Research. Qualifications Guidelines: Any combination of experience/training/education equivalent to, but not limited to, the following: Required • Bachelor's degree preferred; high school diploma required with 1-3 years of related experience. • Demonstrated ability to gather, analyze, interpret, and present complex information from multiple sources. • Ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and maintain confidentiality. Preferred • Experience in prospect research, wealth screening, prospect management, fundraising analytics, or related Advancement functions preferred. • Experience with prospect research resources, wealth screening tools, and fundraising databases preferred. • Knowledge of Slate for Advancement, DonorSearch, LexisNexis, or similar research platforms preferred. • Knowledge of APRA ethical standards and prospect research best practices preferred. Knowledge and Skills • Understanding of higher education and/or nonprofit fundraising environments, particularly Advancement and Development operations. • Strong analytical, critical thinking, and investigative research skills. • Experience with reporting tools, spreadsheets, and data analysis applications. • Advanced written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. • Effective project management skills and ability to analyze and document business processes. Physical Requirements/Working Conditions: Working Conditions: Duties performed are primarily in an office environment while sitting or standing at a desk or computer workstation or in meetings. Health and comfort prioritized. This position requires flexible working hours, which may include working some evenings, weekends, and some holidays. Physical Demands: This position requires sitting for long periods of time, as well as some bending and stooping when working with files. This position does have some limited lifting involved but not more than 10 pounds at a time. Quite a bit of finger/hand dexterity is involved regarding typing and/or filing. The overall setting of the job is in an area conducive to a normal office environment with minimal exposure to adverse conditions. TO APPLY: A resume/CV and cover letter are required. In compliance with The Americans with Disabilities Act, if selected for the interview process and accommodations are needed, please call (909) 748-8040. If you are unable to complete an application due to a disability, contact us at (909) 748-8040 to ask for accommodation or an alternative application process. BACKGROUND CHECK: Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Offers are conditional and may be rescinded if disqualifying information is found or if information was withheld or falsified. Current employees may be affected if the check is not satisfactorily completed. DRIVER’S LICENSE: Certain positions require a valid driver’s license and enrollment in the DMV Government Employer Pull Notice Program to verify license status and driving record. PHYSICAL/PSYCHOLOGICAL EXAMS: Select positions (e.g., Public Safety, Facilities, Student Affairs, Athletics, ITS) require a pre-employment physical exam, including the ability to lift 50+ lbs. Public Safety Officers must also pass a psychological evaluation. FOR MORE INFORMATION VISIT Human Resources (redlands.edu) SUBMISSION OF A RESUME OR APPLICATION INDICATES AGREEMENT THAT THE UNIVERSITY MAY VERIFY ANY AND ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED THEREIN. MEMBERS OF UNDERREPRESENTED GROUPS ARE ENCOURAGED TO APPLY. AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications Equal Opportunity Employer/Protected Veterans/Individuals with Disabilities This employer is required to notify all applicants of their rights pursuant to federal employment laws.\nFor further information, please review the Know Your Rights notice from the Department of Labor. AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
